        "prompt_1": "id=\"x001\"\n\nsubject_definitions:\n<Subject 1>: A heavyset older police chief in his late sixties, broad through the shoulders and waist, weathered face, deep-set tired eyes, heavy grey stubble and short thinning steel-grey hair. He wears a battered charcoal police coat over a rumpled dark shirt, worn trousers and heavy boots. Hardened, unsentimental, physically tired but authoritative.\n<Subject 2>: A rugged woman in her late thirties with a messy dark bob cut, uneven loose strands around her face, weathered features and a guarded observant expression. She wears worn dark brown-black leather outerwear over faded layered clothing, practical trousers and scuffed boots. Quiet, economical movements, minimal speech.\n<Environment 1>: A busy rustic cyberpunk police precinct inside an aging industrial brick building. Battered steel desks are arranged in fixed rows. A broad permanent central aisle runs from the chief's desk area toward a heavy steel-framed exit door. Exposed pipes, hanging cable bundles, scratched terminals, patched fluorescent fixtures, old ventilation fans, warm desk lamps, paper files, chipped paint and smoky atmospheric haze fill the room. Officers work at desks and move through side aisles while the central aisle remains naturally clear. Rain-dark night is visible through dirty windows.\n<Prop or VFX 1>: A battered physical case folder resting on the chief's crowded desk among mugs, handwritten notes and old equipment.\n\nsummary:\nThe chief begins briefing the woman about a domestic synth that murdered the family it belonged to. She listens without interruption and asks only why the assignment has come to her. The conversation remains restrained and adult, with the camera focused on the people rather than explanatory inserts.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1>: newly_generated, persistent identity for x001 through x004.\n<Subject 2>: newly_generated, persistent identity for the full sequence.\n<Environment 1>: newly_generated, persistent precinct environment for x001 through x004.\n<Prop or VFX 1>: newly_generated, persistent through x003.\n\ndetailed_description:\nA shoulder-height medium-wide handheld shot from slightly behind <Subject 2> frames <Subject 1> across the battered steel desk. The composition uses a restrained documentary-style perspective. The broad central aisle is already visible behind <Subject 2>, naturally clear all the way toward the precinct exit.\n\n<Subject 1> sits heavily with one forearm resting beside the closed folder. He studies <Subject 2> for a short beat, pulls the folder toward himself and opens it low on the desk.\n\nThe folder remains incidental to the frame. Its contents are angled away from the camera and partially hidden by his hands, desk clutter and perspective. There are no full-frame document inserts, no audience-facing evidence displays and no readable closeups of paperwork.\n\n(S1) says in a low gravelled voice: \"Got a bad one. Domestic synth. Killed the family it was registered to three nights ago.\"\n\nHe shifts one page with two fingers while speaking.\n\n<Subject 2> glances downward briefly, then returns her attention to his face. Her reaction is restrained: her jaw tightens slightly and one thumb rubs once along the seam of her glove.\n\nBackground officers remain occupied with their own work. Nobody reacts theatrically to the conversation.\n\n(S2) asks: \"Why me?\"\n\n<Subject 1> leans forward and places both forearms on the desk.\n\nContinuity closing state:\n<Subject 1> is leaning forward over the open folder with both forearms on the desk. <Subject 2> remains seated directly opposite him, still and attentive. The broad central aisle behind her remains open and unchanged. No one is standing in her eventual route toward the exit.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nLayered police-station ambience: subdued overlapping conversation, keyboards, paper handling, distant radio chatter, ventilation fans, occasional footsteps and rain against windows. Dialogue remains close and clear.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nNone.",
        "duration_1": 10,
        "overlap_1": 0,
        "prompt_2": "id=\"x002\"\n\nsubject_definitions:\n<Subject 1>: The same heavyset older police chief established in x001, with weathered face, deep-set tired eyes, grey stubble, thinning steel-grey hair and battered charcoal police coat.\n<Subject 2>: The same rugged woman established in x001, with messy dark bob cut, worn leather outerwear and guarded observant expression.\n<Environment 1>: The same rustic cyberpunk police precinct established in x001. The chief's desk remains beside the same broad permanent central aisle leading unobstructed toward the exit. Officers continue working at fixed desks along either side.\n<Prop or VFX 1>: The same battered case folder, containing information about the harbor industrial district and a defunct NVIDIA fabrication plant. The physical pages remain low on the desk and never become audience-facing inserts.\n\nsummary:\nThe chief explains where the synth disappeared and identifies the abandoned NVIDIA fabrication plant. The woman asks whether anyone has already entered. He tells her that two reconnaissance drones were sent and neither returned.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1>: fully_preserved from x001.\n<Subject 2>: fully_preserved from x001.\n<Environment 1>: fully_preserved from x001.\n<Prop or VFX 1>: fully_preserved from x001.\n\ndetailed_description:\nContinuity opening state:\n<Subject 1> is leaning forward over the open folder with both forearms on the desk. <Subject 2> remains seated directly opposite him, still and attentive. The broad central aisle behind her remains open and unchanged. No one is standing in her eventual route toward the exit.\n\nThe camera holds a medium conversational composition across the desk, then performs a restrained slow lateral drift toward <Subject 2>'s side while keeping both faces visible.\n\n<Subject 1> taps one finger against information lying low on the desk.\n\n(S1) says: \"Because patrol lost it in Harbor Nine.\"\n\nHis finger moves a short distance across the physical paperwork.\n\n(S1) continues: \"Thermal trail ended at a defunct NVIDIA fabrication plant. Place has been dead twenty years.\"\n\nThe camera remains at conversational height. The papers stay oblique, partially covered and visually secondary. Do not cut to maps, photographs or documents filling the frame.\n\n<Subject 2> lowers her eyes toward the desk for a moment. A loose strand of her bob falls near one eye and she brushes it aside with the back of one finger.\n\n(S2) asks: \"Anyone go in?\"\n\n<Subject 1> pauses and looks directly at her.\n\n(S1) says: \"Two drones.\"\n\nA radio crackles somewhere deeper in the precinct.\n\n(S1) finishes: \"Neither came back.\"\n\nThe camera settles back into a balanced two-shot.\n\nContinuity closing state:\nBoth characters remain seated across the desk. <Subject 1> sits slightly forward with his hands withdrawn from the paperwork. <Subject 2>'s gaze has returned to his face. The open folder remains low between them. The same broad central aisle behind her remains entirely clear.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nContinuous precinct ambience with low conversation, radio chatter, keyboards, ventilation noise and rain. A brief radio burst occurs during the pause around the missing drones.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nNone.",
        "duration_2": 10,
        "overlap_2": 22,
        "prompt_3": "id=\"x003\"\n\nsubject_definitions:\n<Subject 1>: The same heavyset older police chief established in x001 and x002.\n<Subject 2>: The same rugged woman with messy dark bob cut and worn leather outerwear.\n<Environment 1>: The same rustic cyberpunk police precinct, including the same fixed desk layout and broad unobstructed central aisle.\n<Prop or VFX 1>: The same battered case folder, now partly closed and visually secondary.\n<Prop or VFX 2>: A slim rectangular cyberpunk payment card approximately ordinary credit-card size, worn metallic-polymer construction with a subtle embedded authentication strip. Compact enough to fit naturally in a wallet or jacket pocket.\n<Prop or VFX 3>: A compact encrypted cyberpunk storage device roughly the size of two stacked matchboxes, dark ruggedized casing, beveled metal edges, recessed connector geometry and several tiny status indicators. Clearly advanced future data hardware, not an oversized object and not a modern USB stick.\n\nsummary:\nThe chief gives the operational terms. The woman asks only about payment. He places half the payment and the encrypted mission data on the desk.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1>: fully_preserved from x002.\n<Subject 2>: fully_preserved from x002.\n<Environment 1>: fully_preserved from x002.\n<Prop or VFX 1>: fully_preserved from x002.\n<Prop or VFX 2>: newly_generated.\n<Prop or VFX 3>: newly_generated.\n\ndetailed_description:\nContinuity opening state:\nBoth characters remain seated across the desk. <Subject 1> sits slightly forward with his hands withdrawn from the paperwork. <Subject 2>'s gaze is on his face. The open folder remains low between them. The same broad central aisle behind her remains entirely clear.\n\nThe camera settles into a compact medium two-shot from the corner of the desk.\n\n<Subject 1> folds part of the case folder closed, reducing its visual prominence even further.\n\n(S1) says: \"Go in quiet. Confirm it's there. Shut it down.\"\n\nHe reaches inside his coat and removes <Prop or VFX 2>, the slim payment card. He lays it flat on the desk and pushes it only a short distance toward <Subject 2>.\n\nThe payment card remains normal wallet-card scale. It must not become a coin, giant disk, medallion or oversized token.\n\n<Subject 2> glances at the card.\n\n(S2) asks: \"Pay?\"\n\n(S1) replies: \"Half now. Half when it's cold.\"\n\nHe removes <Prop or VFX 3>, the compact encrypted storage device, and sets it beside the payment card. Several tiny recessed status lights activate briefly.\n\n(S1) adds: \"Everything we have is on that.\"\n\n<Subject 2> places one hand on the desk but stops a few centimeters short of both objects. She studies the chief for a quiet beat.\n\nContinuity closing state:\nThe slim payment card and compact encrypted storage device rest side-by-side directly in front of <Subject 2>. Her hand rests on the desk close to them. <Subject 1> has withdrawn both hands. Both characters remain seated. The broad unobstructed central aisle toward the precinct exit remains clearly visible behind her.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nContinuous precinct room tone. A light flat tap when the payment card touches the desk and a denser metallic-polymer click when the storage device is placed beside it.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nNone.",
