        "prompt_5": "id=\"x005\"\n\nsubject_definitions:\n<Environment 1>: The same precinct exit area established at the end of x004, visible only for the opening continuity beat.\n<Environment 2>: A newly established vast aged cyberpunk city during deep night. The sky is black beneath heavy rainclouds. Layered concrete towers, rust-streaked megastructures, elevated rail lines, rooftop machinery, old neon signage, steam vents and countless mismatched windows extend into dark rain haze. Illumination comes from artificial city light only: fragmented amber sodium lamps, old signage, red warning lights, cold industrial lighting and reflected window glow on rain-wet surfaces.\n<Environment 3>: A newly established harbor industrial district within the same city and during the exact same deep night. Black rain-dimpled harbor water, skeletal loading cranes, rusted pipelines, abandoned warehouses, dead smokestacks and enormous derelict factories line the waterfront beneath a black clouded sky. Sparse sodium lamps, distant city glow and isolated industrial security lights provide the only illumination.\n<Prop or VFX 1>: The defunct NVIDIA fabrication plant within <Environment 3>, a sprawling aging industrial complex of interconnected fabrication halls, utility towers, rooftop ventilation structures, stained concrete and broad abandoned parking areas. Most of the complex is dark. Only a few weak exterior security lamps and dying utility lights remain. A large weather-damaged NVIDIA identity is faintly visible on one exterior structure under artificial night lighting.\n\nsummary:\nThe closed precinct door holds briefly, then hard cuts to a vast cyberpunk city aerial during deep night as aggressive distorted FM-synth music begins. A second hard cut moves to the harbor district during the same night and approaches the abandoned NVIDIA fabrication plant.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Environment 1>: fully_preserved from x004 for the opening continuity state only.\n<Environment 2>: newly_generated.\n<Environment 3>: newly_generated, geographically part of <Environment 2> and preserving the exact same nighttime, weather and atmospheric conditions.\n<Prop or VFX 1>: newly_generated, persistent physical location for x005 onward.\n\ndetailed_description:\nContinuity opening state:\nA static interior view holds on the fully closed steel-framed precinct exit door. <Subject 2> is outside and no longer visible.\n\n[Shot 1]\nHold the closed precinct door for approximately 0.25 seconds.\n\nAt approximately 00:00.250:\n\nHARD CUT TO A NEW ENVIRONMENT AND NEW CAMERA.\n\n[Shot 2]\nAn extreme-wide high-altitude cinematic aerial above <Environment 2>.\n\nIt is unmistakably deep night.\n\nThe black rainclouded sky occupies the upper portion of frame while the city stretches beneath it as an enormous field of scattered artificial illumination. There is no natural ambient daylight character to the image. Buildings emerge from darkness through windows, old signage, rooftop warning lights and pools of industrial illumination.\n\nThe camera glides forward at steady aircraft-like speed while descending slightly.\n\nElevated trains move far below. Steam rises through artificial lighting and disappears into black rain haze. Wet rooftops and streets carry fragmented reflected light.\n\nThe distorted FM-synth score begins on the exact first frame of this aerial.\n\nAt approximately 00:04.500:\n\nHARD CUT TO A DIFFERENT CINEMATIC AERIAL CAMERA.\n\n[Shot 3]\nA lower-altitude aerial is already moving above <Environment 3>, the harbor industrial district.\n\nThe exact nighttime state is preserved across the cut: black clouded sky, dark harbor water, rain haze and artificial illumination only.\n\nThe harbor district is considerably darker than the city center. Huge industrial structures exist mostly as silhouettes, revealed intermittently by isolated sodium lamps, red tower lights and distant city glow reflecting from wet metal.\n\nThe camera moves diagonally above the waterfront.\n\nBlack harbor water occupies one side of frame. Skeletal cranes, pipelines, abandoned fabrication buildings and dead smokestacks pass beneath the camera.\n\nFarther ahead, <Prop or VFX 1>, the defunct NVIDIA fabrication plant, becomes distinguishable from the surrounding industrial blocks.\n\nThe camera gradually adjusts course toward the complex and descends slightly.\n\nA few weak security lamps illuminate portions of exterior walls and wet pavement. Most windows remain completely dark.\n\nThe weathered NVIDIA identity becomes faintly readable only because nearby industrial lighting grazes the old facade.\n\nThe image remains a clean cinematic color aerial.\n\nThere is no HUD, surveillance overlay or drone interface in this prompt.\n\nContinuity closing state:\nA clean nighttime cinematic aerial approaches the abandoned NVIDIA fabrication plant from above and at moderate distance. The factory is centered ahead beside the black harbor. The sky remains black and rainclouded. The surrounding industrial district is dark, illuminated only by sparse artificial lights and distant city glow. No HUD or surveillance graphics are visible.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nDistant nighttime city machinery and aerial traffic during the first aerial. After the harbor cut: coastal wind, rain, black water striking concrete, loose metal rattling and a faint distant electrical hum.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nHardcore distorted dissonant FM-synth cinematic ambience begins abruptly with the first city aerial frame: metallic frequency modulation, unstable digital harmonics, deep sub pressure and irregular industrial percussion.",
